<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<dataModel xmlns="http://xmlns.oracle.com/oxp/xmlp" version="2.1"
           defaultDataSourceRef="ApplicationDB_FSCM">
  <!--
    DMT_TALENT_PROF_RECON_DM — BIP reconciliation report contract v1 for
    TalentProfiles (loaded via HCM Data Loader). Design doc: "BIP reconciliation
    report contract - v1" (nine columns, six parameters, keyset pagination) plus
    its HDL note: "each HDL object gets a Contract v1 report whose rows are the
    BASE tier (key + Fusion id); its ERROR rows are optional because HDL failures
    arrive per-record in the HDL response and are tagged [FUSION_ERROR] before the
    report runs."

    BASE-TIER ONLY. An HDL load has no interface table, so this report returns the
    BASE tier: one row per migrated component that Fusion positively confirmed,
    with a real Fusion base-table id as FUSION_ID. This is the same base-tier proof
    the Salaries / Workers / BenParticipant reconcilers use.

    TWO COMPONENTS, ONE ROW EACH (distinguished by OBJECT_TYPE). The load writes a
    parent TalentProfile.dat and a child ProfileItem.dat (DMT_TALENT_PROF_HDL_GEN_PKG):
      * ProfileItem   SourceSystemId = (prefixed PERSON_NUMBER) || '_TPITM'
      * TalentProfile SourceSystemId = (prefixed PERSON_NUMBER) || '_TPROF'
    both with SourceSystemOwner 'HRC_SQLLOADER'. The transform stamps both as
    RECON_KEY on their TFM rows (DMT_TALENT_PROF_TRANSFORM_PKG).

    HOW THIS OBJECT ACTUALLY LANDS IN THE KEY MAP (verified live 2026-09-20,
    fin_impl / ApplicationDB_FSCM — see the honest notes below):
      * The ONLY HRC_SQLLOADER-owned talent object present in
        HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP is OBJECT_NAME='ProfileItem' (4 rows on the pod).
        There is NO HRC_SQLLOADER 'Profile'/'TalentProfile' key-map row: this HDL
        path registers a key map entry for the CHILD item only, not for the parent
        profile. So the child is the anchor, and the parent is reached through it.
      * ProfileItem SURROGATE_ID = HRT_PROFILE_ITEMS.PROFILE_ITEM_ID — proven by
        joining all 4 back to the base table. Each item's HRT_PROFILE_ITEMS.PROFILE_ID
        round-trips to a real HRT_PROFILES_B row (PROFILE_CODE 'PERS_<profile_id>'),
        so the parent profile is provably in its base table too.

    RESULTING TWO ROWS PER MIGRATED ITEM:
      * OBJECT_TYPE='ProfileItem',   RECORD_KEY = item SourceSystemId,
        FUSION_ID = HRT_PROFILE_ITEMS.PROFILE_ITEM_ID.
      * OBJECT_TYPE='TalentProfile', RECORD_KEY = 'PROF:' || PROFILE_ID,
        FUSION_ID = HRT_PROFILES_B.PROFILE_ID (one row per distinct parent profile).

    BASE-TABLE NOTE. HRT_PROFILE_ITEMS and HRT_PROFILES_B are selectable by name
    from the BIP reporting user (the *_B item variant HRT_PROFILE_ITEMS_B and *_VL
    are NOT — ORA-00942). This report joins the key map to HRT_PROFILE_ITEMS so
    every FUSION_ID it returns is a verified base-table id, not a bare SURROGATE_ID.

    HONEST STATUS OF THE RECONCILER ROUND-TRIP. The live key-map rows predate the
    current _TPROF/_TPITM SourceSystemId format (they are earlier discovery/seed
    loads: '10554DMTTP001', 'DMTTP-SEED-1'); there are ZERO %_TPROF / %_TPITM rows
    on the pod yet. The standalone proof below therefore uses the live prefix
    '10554' data that exists; a full reconciler round-trip (RECORD_KEY == the TFM
    RECON_KEY of a real gen-package run) awaits a fresh TalentProfiles run whose
    key-map rows carry the _TPITM suffix. The reconciler itself is NOT modified by
    this change.

    NINE response columns, in contract order:
      OBJECT_TYPE, RECORD_KEY, SOURCE_TYPE('BASE'), FUSION_STATUS('SUCCESS'),
      FUSION_ID (verified base id), ERROR_MESSAGE (NULL), LOAD_REQUEST_ID (NULL),
      SOURCE_REF (= RECORD_KEY), DMT_REFERENCE (NULL).
    SIX parameters: P_RUN_ID, P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID, P_IMPORT_ESS_ID, P_PREFIX,
      P_CHUNK_SIZE, P_AFTER_KEY.
    KEYSET pagination by RECORD_KEY (P_AFTER_KEY cursor, P_CHUNK_SIZE page).
      Base-tier matching is by run prefix (P_PREFIX). LOAD_REQUEST_ID /
      P_IMPORT_ESS_ID do not survive into the base for an HDL load, so they are not
      filters; LOAD_REQUEST_ID is returned NULL per the contract column mapping.
  -->
  <dataProperties>
    <property name="include_parameters" value="true"/>
    <property name="include_null_Element" value="true"/>
    <property name="include_rowsettag" value="false"/>
    <property name="xml_tag_case" value="upper"/>
  </dataProperties>
  <dataSets>
    <dataSet name="talent_prof_recon" type="complex">
      <sql dataSourceRef="ApplicationDB_FSCM"><![CDATA[
SELECT
    object_type, record_key, source_type, fusion_status,
    fusion_id, error_message, load_request_id, source_ref, dmt_reference
FROM (
    -- Child component: one HRC_INTEGRATION_KEY_MAP row per ProfileItem
    -- (OBJECT_NAME='ProfileItem', SOURCE_SYSTEM_OWNER='HRC_SQLLOADER'); its
    -- SURROGATE_ID is the HRT_PROFILE_ITEMS.PROFILE_ITEM_ID (join proves the base
    -- row exists and yields the parent PROFILE_ID for the parent component).
    SELECT 'ProfileItem'                  AS object_type,
           m.source_system_id             AS record_key,
           'BASE'                         AS source_type,
           'SUCCESS'                      AS fusion_status,
           i.profile_item_id              AS fusion_id,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))   AS error_message,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(30))     AS load_request_id,
           m.source_system_id             AS source_ref,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))   AS dmt_reference
    FROM   hrc_integration_key_map m
    JOIN   hrt_profile_items i
           ON i.profile_item_id = m.surrogate_id
    WHERE  m.object_name         = 'ProfileItem'
    AND    m.source_system_owner = 'HRC_SQLLOADER'
    AND    m.source_system_id LIKE :P_PREFIX || '%'
    UNION ALL
    -- Parent component: the distinct talent profile behind the migrated items,
    -- confirmed in HRT_PROFILES_B by its PROFILE_ID (reached via the item).
    -- One row per distinct parent profile in this run's prefix.
    SELECT 'TalentProfile'               AS object_type,
           'PROF:' || i.profile_id        AS record_key,
           'BASE'                         AS source_type,
           'SUCCESS'                      AS fusion_status,
           MAX(i.profile_id)              AS fusion_id,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))   AS error_message,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(30))     AS load_request_id,
           'PROF:' || i.profile_id        AS source_ref,
           CAST(NULL AS VARCHAR2(4000))   AS dmt_reference
    FROM   hrc_integration_key_map m
    JOIN   hrt_profile_items i
           ON i.profile_item_id = m.surrogate_id
    WHERE  m.object_name         = 'ProfileItem'
    AND    m.source_system_owner = 'HRC_SQLLOADER'
    AND    m.source_system_id LIKE :P_PREFIX || '%'
    GROUP BY i.profile_id
)
-- Keyset predicate. An empty P_AFTER_KEY (first page) binds to NULL in BIP, so
-- treat NULL as "from the start": every non-null RECORD_KEY sorts after the empty
-- string. On later pages P_AFTER_KEY carries the previous page's last RECORD_KEY
-- and only greater keys are returned.
WHERE  (:P_AFTER_KEY IS NULL OR record_key > :P_AFTER_KEY)
ORDER BY record_key
FETCH FIRST :P_CHUNK_SIZE ROWS ONLY
      ]]></sql>
    </dataSet>
  </dataSets>
  <output rootName="DATA_DS" uniqueRowName="false">
    <nodeList name="data-structure">
      <dataStructure tagName="DATA_DS">
        <group name="G_1" label="G_1" source="talent_prof_recon">
          <element name="OBJECT_TYPE"     value="OBJECT_TYPE"     dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="OBJECT_TYPE"/>
          <element name="RECORD_KEY"      value="RECORD_KEY"      dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="RECORD_KEY"/>
          <element name="SOURCE_TYPE"     value="SOURCE_TYPE"     dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="SOURCE_TYPE"/>
          <element name="FUSION_STATUS"   value="FUSION_STATUS"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="FUSION_STATUS"/>
          <element name="FUSION_ID"       value="FUSION_ID"       dataType="xsd:integer" tagName="FUSION_ID"/>
          <element name="ERROR_MESSAGE"   value="ERROR_MESSAGE"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="ERROR_MESSAGE"/>
          <element name="LOAD_REQUEST_ID" value="LOAD_REQUEST_ID" dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="LOAD_REQUEST_ID"/>
          <element name="SOURCE_REF"      value="SOURCE_REF"      dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="SOURCE_REF"/>
          <element name="DMT_REFERENCE"   value="DMT_REFERENCE"   dataType="xsd:string"  tagName="DMT_REFERENCE"/>
        </group>
      </dataStructure>
    </nodeList>
  </output>
  <eventTriggers/>
  <lexicals/>
  <parameters>
    <parameter name="P_RUN_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_RUN_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_LOAD_REQUEST_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_IMPORT_ESS_ID" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_IMPORT_ESS_ID" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_PREFIX" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_PREFIX" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <!-- Keyset pagination: page size + cursor. The reconciler calls with an empty
         P_AFTER_KEY first, then passes the last RECORD_KEY received on each next
         call, until a short page returns. -->
    <parameter name="P_CHUNK_SIZE" dataType="integer" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_CHUNK_SIZE" defaultValue="5000" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
    <parameter name="P_AFTER_KEY" dataType="character" rowPlacement="1"
               labelID="P_AFTER_KEY" defaultValue="" nvp="false"
               refreshParamOnChange="false" useNullForAll="false"/>
  </parameters>
  <valueSets/>
  <bursting/>
</dataModel>
